{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/112207-wod-dot-rating-html5-widget","id":112207,"title":"WoD dot rating HTML5 widget","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-13T13:16:05-07:00","id":112207,"title":"WoD dot rating HTML5 widget","content":"For sometime I've been trying to create a solid, beautiful and responsive website that will act as an online character sheet/database for the WoD/cWoD games. The most tough part on these experiments was making a proper dot rating widget/component and after many tries I think I got it right!<br /> <br /> Also I thought I shouldn't keep that to myself and let it open for anyone that needs it. So this is the url to download it <a href=\"https://github.com/ragecryx/Storytelling-System-Dot-Rating-Widget\" target=\"_blank\">https://github.com/ragecryx/Storytel...-Rating-Widget</a> and here to check it live <a href=\"http://goo.gl/Eha8PQ\" target=\"_blank\">http://goo.gl/Eha8PQ</a>. Any feedback, suggestions for improvements or fixes are more than welcome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/405-ragecryx","name":"ragecryx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar405_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T15:01:01-07:00","id":112255,"title":"","content":"Very slick, nice work. <br /> <br /> Setting the Skill to zero dots felt a little awkward at first because it wasn't clear where I needed to click. Do I click the single filled-in dot to toggle it? Is there an area to the left of it I click? It's a minor thing, since once you figure it it's ease to use. <br /> <br /> However, if you felt like tinkering more, you could try adding a visual indicator for when zero would be active. One way is to set the cursor. On my system, at least, it shows a hand when I'm hovering over a valid dot to click on. It doesn't show the hand if I'm in a position to click for zero dots, but having it do that (only for widgets that allow zero) would help. Instead, or in addition, you could have the element as a whole highlight subtly whenever you're hovered over a valid choice.<br /> <br /> For reference, I tried it using FF 28 on Windows 7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T23:47:32-07:00","id":112456,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> The rating is set to zero dots when you click on the rating but not on a particular dot (e.g. on the title of the rating) and it is kinda confusing indeed, but I didn't want to add buttons or something like this, because I thought the point is to be as close to the paper as possible. Maybe to make the leftmost dot like a toggle? if you click it and its already marked it will unmark it?<br /> <br /> Also I'm planning to add squared versions for Health/Willpower etc, and maybe a way of adding 1-2 lines description for each dot rating that will appear when you hover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/405-ragecryx","name":"ragecryx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar405_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T06:47:13-07:00","id":115819,"title":"","content":"I just added the squared version with &quot;X&quot; for marking. Will be working on the visual indication for cleaning the dots and a version for health with / X and * markings.<br /> <br /> You can check the changes <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/62860879/Storytelling%20System%20-%20HTML5%20Dot%20Component/example.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/405-ragecryx","user":"ragecryx","date":".  Added link for preview 04-19-2014, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/405-ragecryx","name":"ragecryx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar405_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T08:28:13-07:00","id":123173,"title":"","content":"I suggests you group your dots in groups of 5. It will be visually easier for users to count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T03:00:53-07:00","id":125094,"title":"","content":"Done! Added a small space per 5 dots. Preview <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/62860879/Storytelling%20System%20-%20HTML5%20Dot%20Component/example.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> Thanks for the feedback Chattnos!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/405-ragecryx","name":"ragecryx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar405_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T01:55:51-07:00","id":128084,"title":"","content":"This looks good, straightforward and easy to use. Thanks for sharing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">A monster by any other name...</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1204-bridgewarden","name":"BridgeWarden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1204_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T13:42:29-07:00","id":134302,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I'm also working on a web-based character sheet that will use the widget but I think its too soon to show it at this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/405-ragecryx","user":"ragecryx","date":". 05-12-2014, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.co